1. High-Level Architecture Overview
CloudBees CI will run entirely on Amazon EKS, with the following components:
Control Plane
Managed EKS control plane (AWS-managed)
Multi-AZ deployment
Compute
Worker nodes (managed node groups)
Options:
On-Demand
Spot (for build agents only)
CloudBees Components
Operations Center (OC) – central management
Managed Controllers (MC) – separate controllers per team/project
Build Agents – ephemeral Kubernetes pods
Shared Libraries – stored in Git
Service Cloud integrations – Webhooks, SCM, etc.
2. Architecture Components (Detailed)
a) EKS Cluster (Multi-AZ)
Version: EKS 1.29+ (recommended)
Node groups:
System Node Group → OC + MCs
Build Agent Node Group → EC2 or Fargate (optional)
b) Storage
EBS CSI → PersistentVolumes for:
Operations Center
Managed Controllers
S3 → Backups, artifacts, configuration archive
c) Build Agents
Kubernetes pod-based agents
Autoscaled using:
Horizontal Pod Autoscaler
Cluster Autoscaler
Agents run in separate namespaces or dedicated node pools
d) Networking
VPC with private subnets for controllers
NLB / ALB exposed via:
ingress-nginx OR
AWS Load Balancer Controller
DNS:
Route53 → ci.company.com
Ingress uses:
TLS termination (ACM certificate)
e) Security
IAM roles:
IRSA for controllers & pods
Least privilege model
Secrets management:
AWS Secrets Manager OR
Kubernetes Secrets (encrypted by KMS)
Authentication:
SSO / SAML (Okta / AD) integrated with CloudBees Ops Center
RBAC mapped to groups
f) Observability
Logging:
CloudWatch Container Insights
Fluent Bit DaemonSet
Monitoring:
Prometheus + Grafana
or
CloudWatch metrics (EKS native)
Alerts:
SNS / Slack / PagerDuty
